189 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Udyoga Pramoda\nDesigning a Mentor\055Gated Progression System to Structure a Volunteer\055Driven Career Platform\nUdyoga Pramoda is a community\055led career initiative where senior professionals mentor early\055career aspirants through skill workshops\054 resume reviews\054 and interview preparation\056\nAs participation scaled\054 coordination relied heavily on WhatsApp and informal communication\056 Readiness validation existed\054 but it was not structured\054 visible\054 or measurable\056 Placements were happening\054 but there was no way to track progression or analyze outcomes systematically\056\nI designed a lightweight mentor\055gated progression system that structured informal validation into a measurable readiness funnel\024without increasing mentor burden\056\nContext\nThe initiative grew to 150\053 active aspirants\056\nAt this scale\072\nMentor validation lived in chats and memory\nNo centralized aspirant tracking existed\nReadiness stages were not visible\nAdministrators lacked funnel clarity\nPlacement outcomes were anecdotal\nThe system functioned\054 but it was fragile and not scalable\056\nThis was not a UI polish problem\056\050 It was an operational governance problem\056\nThe Product Challenge\nHow might we make mentor\055controlled readiness visible and measurable while preserving the flexibility of a volunteer\055driven ecosystem\077\nThe solution needed to introduce structure without introducing bureaucracy\056\nKey Insight\nPlacement strongly correlated with mentor\055validated readiness\056\nOut of 150 aspirants\072\n50 completed mentor\055assigned skill tasks and were validated as job\055ready\n25\053 secured placements within 3 months\n\17650\045 conversion from validated aspirants to placement\nAverage salary\072 \176\2717\0565 LPA\nThis revealed a structural insight\072\nThe bottleneck was not placement matching\056\050 The bottleneck was readiness conversion \050150 \222 50\051\056\nDesign Approach\nInstead of adding more features\054 I focused on progression logic and visibility\056\nThe objective was to\072\nStructure mentor validation\nReduce coordination ambiguity\nCreate measurable readiness checkpoints\nEnable funnel visibility\nMentor\055Gated Progression\nMentor\055gated progression means aspirants advance only after mentor validation\054 ensuring readiness reflects demonstrated capability rather than self\055declaration\056\nIn practice\072\nWorkshops and skill tasks acted as readiness checkpoints\nMentors validated completion\nOnly validated aspirants progressed to job applications\nMentor authority already existed\056\050 The platform surfaced and structured it\056\nBefore vs After\nBefore\nValidation through WhatsApp\nNo centralized aspirant list\nReadiness invisible to administrators\nNo measurable funnel\nAfter\nCentralized aspirant tracking\nStructured task checkpoints\nVisible readiness status\nReadiness\055to\055placement conversion measurable\nThe system moved from informal coordination to structured visibility\056\nVolunteer Capacity as a Design Constraint\nMentors were senior professionals contributing voluntarily\056\nThe system had to\072\nAvoid increasing review workload\nMinimize administrative overhead\nPreserve informal mentorship dynamics\nDesign principle followed\072\nNever increase mentor effort per aspirant\056\nStructure was introduced without adding friction\056\nSystem Trade\055offs\nIncreasing readiness aggressively risks\072\nMentor overload\nReduced validation quality\nWeakened placement conversion\nThe system balances\072\nStructure and flexibility\nAccountability and volunteer capacity\nQuantity and signal quality\nOutcomes\n150 aspirants onboarded\n50 mentor\055validated as job\055ready \05033\045\051\n25\053 secured placements \050\17650\045 conversion from validated\051\nAverage salary \176\2717\0565 LPA\nReduced coordination ambiguity\nImproved funnel visibility\nMost importantly\054 mentor\055controlled progression became measurable without becoming bureaucratic\056\nReflection\nThe core value of this project was not in interface design\054 but in structuring informal mentor\055driven progression into a scalable\054 trackable system\056\nFuture opportunity lies in improving readiness conversion without increasing mentor burden\024through better pre\055validation and clearer next\055step guidance\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 192 0 R
     /Pg 188 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
